yeah In `torch/_inductor/fx_passes/overlap_manual_scheduling.py`, `merge_all_gather_bucket` embeds `dist.get_rank()` as a compile-time constant into the traced FX graph (calculating rank-specific narrow offsets into the all-gather output buffer).

When `ManualOverlapScheduler` is registered as a custom post-grad pass (e.g. via `config.post_grad_custom_post_pass`), global configs like `bucket_all_gathers_fx `and `enable_overlap_scheduling` are not set. Without a` CustomGraphModulePass` wrapper that supplies a rank-aware `uuid()`, `FxGraphHashDetails._get_custom_pass_detail` produces identical cache keys across ranks, causing warm `FxGraphCache` collisions where non-zero ranks load rank 0's compiled binary.

